@@ -1,0 +2,7 @@ [A]
+
+**Wake compatibility.** Upstream `/loop` denotes event wakeups or a timed heartbeat. No equivalent command is verified in this Codex surface. Use an actually exposed, authorized wake facility with those semantics, or report the unattended step blocked. A native subagent completion notification alone does not provide periodic or restart-persistent execution.
+
+**Codex execution gap.** This playbook retains upstream requirements for isolated cloud workers and independent live verification. Native Codex subagents are session-scoped and share the selected environment; they do not automatically supply isolated cloud workers or one VM per lane. Before executing a cloud-dependent step, verify an authorized adapter provides its required cloud execution, isolation, status, and wake behavior. Without it, report that step blocked and preserve its gates. Do not replace this workflow with a different coordinator architecture.
+
+**External skill dependency.** `cursor-team-kit` is an upstream plugin, not a bundled Codex capability. Use its named skills only if actually installed and compatible. Otherwise report the missing dependency and perform the stated review or runtime proof with available tools; a missing proof remains a gap, never a passed gate.
